      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t have a problem with this approach, but would it be more future-proof to stick -D_GNU_SOURCE in our CPPFLAGS in Makefile.toolchain?\n\nIdeally we want to avoid _GNU_SOURCE completely since the purpose of it is to enable non-standard functionality. For that reason I\u0027d prefer to avoid adding it to the global flags for the whole build.\n\nHere\u0027s the reason why it\u0027s defined for C++: https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/libstdc++/faq.html#faq.predefined",
